WEBVTT

1
00:00:43.808 --> 00:00:45.266
♪ You'll know the right words

2
00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:47.349
♪ They're all in your head

3
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.599
♪ So wake up in the morning
and get out of bed

4
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.432
♪ The dreams
you've been dreaming

5
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.349
♪ Well. right now's the time

6
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:56.016
♪ You build up these monsters

7
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.766
♪ They're just in your mind

8
00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.682
♪ If you feel it in your heart

9
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.766
♪ Then sing it loud

10
00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:04.932
♪ Oh. oh. oh Oh. oh. oh

11
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.516
♪ I know you know who you are
So sing it loud

12
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:11.224
♪ It's all about you

13
00:01:11.392 --> 00:01:14.766
♪ You just gotta know.
gotta know

14
00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:18.516
♪ You can do it on your own

15
00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:20.641
♪ Guess that's why
I wrote this song... ♪

16
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.307
♪ You know it's about you
It's always about you

17
00:01:25.475 --> 00:01:27.349
♪ So let it go. ♪

18
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.641
Bye-bye. orphanage!

19
00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:38.932
Slowly! Almost there!

20
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.224
Stop!

21
00:01:45.308 --> 00:01:48.016
- Shhh!
- Ha!

22
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:52.432
Where is Felicie?

23
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.849
Uh. sir. I don't know.

24
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:57.599
What are you looking at.
you idiot?

25
00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.182
Whoa!

26
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.641
Go get Felicie!

27
00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:05.557
You know. I'm having
a little bit of trouble

28
00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.057
knowing which direction...

29
00:02:07.225 --> 00:02:08.849
Ugh!

30
00:02:13.392 --> 00:02:16.266
Ouch! Ah!

31
00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:23.432
Victor!

32
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.432
- Can you help me?
- Ha!

33
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.432
Stop! Stop doing
your grumpy face!

34
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.349
I'm not. I'm just a little bit hurt
that you were...

35
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:36.182
...I don't know.
escaping without me!

36
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.266
Escaping? Me?

37
00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:43.724
No. I was just looking
at the spectacular view!

38
00:02:43.892 --> 00:02:45.766
Because. you know.
you wouldn't last

39
00:02:45.933 --> 00:02:48.224
more than five minutes
out there without me.

40
00:02:48.392 --> 00:02:50.724
Ha! Ha!

41
00:02:52.517 --> 00:02:54.724
Don't start!
You know how this ends.

42
00:02:54.892 --> 00:02:56.474
We arrived at the same time.

43
00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.307
and we'll escape
at the same time.

44
00:02:58.475 --> 00:02:59.849
I promise!

45
00:03:00.017 --> 00:03:03.391
OK!

46
00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:06.349
Hey. Victor! Hiyah!

47
00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:09.891
Oh. no! Here we go!

48
00:03:10.058 --> 00:03:15.807
Whoo! Whoo!

49
00:03:25.308 --> 00:03:26.849
Whoo!

50
00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.932
♪ You just gotta know.
gotta know

51
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.016
♪ You can do it on your own

52
00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:40.224
♪ This is why I wrote this song

53
00:03:40.392 --> 00:03:42.599
♪ You know it's about you... ♪

54
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.432
- Whoo-hoo!
- ♪ So let it go. ♪

55
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.349
This is the last time!

56
00:03:54.517 --> 00:03:55.891
- We're sorry!
- We're sorry. and...

57
00:03:56.058 --> 00:03:58.891
Tut-tut-tut! Let them go!
You. go to your room.

58
00:03:59.058 --> 00:04:00.932
Thank you!
Thank you. Mother Superior.

59
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.474
Enough. Go to your room.

60
00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.557
And may I just say
that you are looking very...

61
00:04:04.725 --> 00:04:06.682
- Enough.
- ..superior today.

62
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.224
- Enough!
- OK!

63
00:04:08.392 --> 00:04:11.474
Felicie. I know you have
this dream of being a dancer.

64
00:04:11.642 --> 00:04:13.099
- We all know it!
- But I...

65
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.891
Tut-tut-tut!
All the world has a dream.

66
00:04:16.058 --> 00:04:19.141
But get this into your head -
dreams are not reality.

67
00:04:19.308 --> 00:04:21.516
Dreams are buried
because life is

68
00:04:21.683 --> 00:04:23.682
hard. brutal and without pity.

69
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.224
- But...
- Tut-tut-tut!

70
00:04:25.392 --> 00:04:26.432
Agreed?

71
00:04:28.517 --> 00:04:30.057
Agreed.

72
00:04:38.058 --> 00:04:40.516
A dance school in Paris.
little lady.

73
00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:42.182
the Opera de Paris.

74
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.557
full of dancers and dance!

75
00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:47.266
Where did you find this?

76
00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:49.391
I have my sources. OK? Enough!

77
00:04:49.558 --> 00:04:51.307
- Can I see it again?
- No.

78
00:04:51.475 --> 00:04:53.307
Please!

79
00:04:53.475 --> 00:04:56.557
No. but if you escape with me tonight.
you have my word.

80
00:04:56.725 --> 00:04:58.224
I will take you
to this dance school.

81
00:04:58.392 --> 00:05:00.307
and you will become
the greatest dancer.

82
00:05:00.475 --> 00:05:03.974
and I will become
the greatest inventor ever!

83
00:05:04.142 --> 00:05:06.932
- Do you have a plan?
- A brilliant plan!

84
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.974
A plan worthy of my total.
utter. unquestionable genius.

85
00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:11.682
- Let me see.
- After we escape.

86
00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.224
- Now! Now!
- No!

87
00:05:13.392 --> 00:05:14.349
- I said after.
- Now!

88
00:05:14.517 --> 00:05:15.391
- After!
- Now!

89
00:05:15.558 --> 00:05:17.599
- After!
- Ow!

90
00:05:18.808 --> 00:05:21.432
A dance school in Paris.

91
00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.932
Hmm.

92
00:06:06.392 --> 00:06:08.391
Shhh! It's me! Come on!

93
00:06:08.558 --> 00:06:10.141
Oh. my!

94
00:06:10.308 --> 00:06:12.349
Is a chicken part of
your brilliant plan?

95
00:06:12.517 --> 00:06:15.182
- Affirmative!
- Great!

96
00:06:21.392 --> 00:06:23.849
Aaah!

97
00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.682
I'm taking this pitiful deserter

98
00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.932
to Mother Superior.

99
00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.557
OK. Sister. Hmm...

100
00:06:35.725 --> 00:06:37.016
Hmm?

101
00:06:37.183 --> 00:06:38.557
Ahh!

102
00:06:38.725 --> 00:06:41.349
Emergency! Emergency!
Activate Plan B!

103
00:06:41.517 --> 00:06:43.016
- This way!
- Activate Plan B!

104
00:06:43.183 --> 00:06:44.557
That was your best ever plan?

105
00:06:44.725 --> 00:06:46.099
You are so critical!

106
00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:47.724
And you're a terrible escaper!

107
00:06:47.892 --> 00:06:49.557
'Escaper' is not a word!

108
00:06:49.725 --> 00:06:52.599
Ow! God. not again!

109
00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:55.599
Get back down here!

110
00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.266
Open this door!

111
00:06:59.975 --> 00:07:01.932
For the last three months.

112
00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.849
I have been studying chickens.

113
00:07:04.017 --> 00:07:06.307
- I know how they eat.
- Open this door!

114
00:07:06.475 --> 00:07:08.141
I know how they walk.

115
00:07:08.308 --> 00:07:09.932
I know how they lay an egg.

116
00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:14.557
There is nothing about a chicken
that I do not know!

117
00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:17.349
Ta-da!

118
00:07:17.517 --> 00:07:21.557
I call them chicken wings!

119
00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:26.349
Chickens don't fly!

120
00:07:26.517 --> 00:07:29.724
But they have wings.
They must fly.

121
00:07:29.892 --> 00:07:32.432
You fly. don't you?

122
00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:35.516
Fly!

123
00:07:35.683 --> 00:07:38.016
Uh-oh!

124
00:07:38.183 --> 00:07:40.349
I'm going to... Grrr!

125
00:07:40.517 --> 00:07:45.099
Come here. you rascals!

126
00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:46.807
- Goodbye!
- What?

127
00:07:46.975 --> 00:07:49.641
Let's go!

128
00:07:53.558 --> 00:07:55.266
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

129
00:07:59.683 --> 00:08:03.391
One day.
everyone will travel like this!

130
00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.016
Ow!

131
00:08:14.183 --> 00:08:16.724
My music box!

132
00:08:21.017 --> 00:08:22.891
Victor! He's behind you!

133
00:08:23.058 --> 00:08:27.391
I've got my eye on you!
You're not going anywhere!

134
00:08:41.142 --> 00:08:43.807
Aaah! Oh no!

135
00:09:00.308 --> 00:09:02.724
Hang on!

136
00:09:06.933 --> 00:09:07.974
Thanks!

137
00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.016
Victor. watch out!

138
00:09:15.517 --> 00:09:19.974
Yeah! Ha-ha! Now I've got you!

139
00:09:29.517 --> 00:09:32.682
I see you!

140
00:09:39.475 --> 00:09:41.516
This way! Let's go!

141
00:09:53.517 --> 00:09:55.432
- Wait!
- Oh! Oh. no!

142
00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.016
- Yah!
- Grab on! Grab on!

143
00:09:59.183 --> 00:10:02.141
- Oh! Let me go!
- Let him go!

144
00:10:02.308 --> 00:10:06.266
Let me go. stinky! Oh!

145
00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.682
That went well. no?

146
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.599
You're unbelievable.

147
00:10:21.767 --> 00:10:23.391
I know.

148
00:10:23.558 --> 00:10:25.682
Victor. we actually did it!

149
00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.182
Yes. we actually did!

150
00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.891
Oh.

151
00:10:32.892 --> 00:10:34.557
I can fix this.

152
00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.182
But I should say

153
00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.932
that seeing as this
is the one thing

154
00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.391
that was in your crib when you
were left outside the orphanage.

155
00:10:43.558 --> 00:10:46.974
you should take
a teeny-tiny. eensy-weensy

156
00:10:47.142 --> 00:10:50.224
little bit more care of it.

157
00:10:50.392 --> 00:10:53.307
Fixed! Don't thank me!

158
00:10:53.475 --> 00:10:57.391
And tomorrow. chérie. Paris...

159
00:11:00.308 --> 00:11:01.849
...will be ours.

160
00:11:29.017 --> 00:11:31.807
Good morning. sunshine!

161
00:11:31.975 --> 00:11:35.391
Eww! When's the last time
you brushed your teeth?

162
00:11:35.558 --> 00:11:37.641
Start with this one.

163
00:11:37.808 --> 00:11:38.849
Whoa!

164
00:11:51.725 --> 00:11:53.266
Ugh!

165
00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.682
I can't see where we are.

166
00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.516
Relax! We're in Paris! Aaah!

167
00:12:02.683 --> 00:12:04.391
Quiet! We're
going to get caught!

168
00:12:04.558 --> 00:12:05.932
Not another noise out of you.

169
00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.516
That wasn't me!

170
00:12:15.392 --> 00:12:16.807
Wow!

171
00:12:16.975 --> 00:12:20.016
- It's incredible!
- Paris is amazing.

172
00:12:30.017 --> 00:12:31.807
So. where's the dance school?

173
00:12:31.975 --> 00:12:33.432
Relax. Felicie!

174
00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.391
Enjoy Paris. Breathe it in.

175
00:12:35.558 --> 00:12:36.932
Hi there!

176
00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.724
Love your moustache. monsieur!

177
00:12:38.892 --> 00:12:41.432
Ah. yes. Paris!

178
00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.307
City of romance. City of dreams.

179
00:12:44.475 --> 00:12:46.557
City of fame and fortune!

180
00:12:46.725 --> 00:12:50.599
City of lamp posts.
City of pigeons.

181
00:12:50.767 --> 00:12:52.682
Did I say romance?

182
00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.807
Yes. you did.
Now. where's the dance school?

183
00:12:54.975 --> 00:12:57.557
Uh. I don't know.

184
00:12:57.725 --> 00:13:00.099
Don't worry. We're a team.

185
00:13:00.267 --> 00:13:03.599
- We'll find it together.
- Ugh!

186
00:13:04.808 --> 00:13:06.807
Do you think it was stupid
to come to Paris?

187
00:13:06.975 --> 00:13:10.307
Don't say that! We should
never give up on our dreams.

188
00:13:13.725 --> 00:13:16.099
We're kids! We're all alone.

189
00:13:16.267 --> 00:13:19.682
Was I really crazy to think
I could be a dancer?

190
00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.349
What do you think?

191
00:13:21.517 --> 00:13:23.932
Victor?

192
00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.057
I said...

193
00:13:26.225 --> 00:13:28.307
Victor?

194
00:13:28.475 --> 00:13:30.807
- I'm OK!
- Come back!

195
00:13:30.975 --> 00:13:32.682
I can't swim!

196
00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:36.266
Meet me on this bridge
at this time tomorrow.

197
00:13:36.433 --> 00:13:38.557
No matter how dangerous it is.

198
00:13:38.725 --> 00:13:41.057
I will return!

199
00:13:42.683 --> 00:13:46.224
Victor! Come back!

200
00:13:46.392 --> 00:13:49.141
Don't leave!

201
00:13:49.308 --> 00:13:50.974
Please.

202
00:14:05.308 --> 00:14:06.849
Huh?

203
00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.682
Aaah!

204
00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.391
What have you come
here to do. huh?

205
00:16:15.558 --> 00:16:17.307
You came here to steal.
didn't you?

206
00:16:17.475 --> 00:16:19.099
Answer me! You're a thief!

207
00:16:19.267 --> 00:16:22.307
I wasn't stealing!
I was looking at the dancer!

208
00:16:22.475 --> 00:16:24.932
Liar! Empty your pockets!

209
00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.599
- Get off me!
- Oh. yeah?

210
00:16:26.767 --> 00:16:28.932
Leave her alone.

211
00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.849
She came here to steal!

212
00:16:31.017 --> 00:16:33.807
I didn't! I really didn't!

213
00:16:33.975 --> 00:16:35.807
Think this through.

214
00:16:35.975 --> 00:16:38.182
If you hurt her.
then you will have to explain

215
00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.682
how she got here
in the first place.

216
00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.557
and aren't you supposed to be
taking care of the building?

217
00:16:44.725 --> 00:16:47.974
Do you really want
to take the fall for this?

218
00:16:56.017 --> 00:16:57.557
Clear off.

219
00:17:00.017 --> 00:17:02.891
- Wait!
- Go. Get out of here.

220
00:17:31.433 --> 00:17:33.807
I have nothing to steal!

221
00:17:33.975 --> 00:17:36.057
I... I can't sp...
I can't speak!

222
00:17:36.225 --> 00:17:38.724
I just wanted to say
thank you for saving me!

223
00:17:38.892 --> 00:17:40.557
You've said it.
Have a nice life.

224
00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.932
Excuse me. but who was
that dancer on stage?

225
00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.682
Rosita Mauri.
top dancer at the Opera.

226
00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:52.349
Wow!

227
00:17:52.517 --> 00:17:56.182
And what she did - that crazy
jumpy thing. what was that?

228
00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:58.766
Are you a dancer too?

229
00:17:58.933 --> 00:18:01.266
I'm a cleaner.
and you are an irritation.

230
00:18:01.433 --> 00:18:03.724
Go away.

231
00:18:03.892 --> 00:18:06.182
But you're the first person

232
00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.224
to show me any kindness
in this city.

233
00:18:08.392 --> 00:18:11.057
I've been separated
from my best friend.

234
00:18:11.225 --> 00:18:13.016
I have nowhere to go.

235
00:18:13.183 --> 00:18:15.349
and I'm an orphan.

236
00:18:15.517 --> 00:18:18.974
Nice try. but I hate kids.

237
00:18:19.142 --> 00:18:21.141
especially orphans.

238
00:18:21.308 --> 00:18:23.182
Go find another idiot.

239
00:18:34.725 --> 00:18:36.349
The stairs. Odette.

240
00:18:36.517 --> 00:18:38.057
The stairs are a disgrace.

241
00:18:38.225 --> 00:18:39.599
I have guests
tomorrow afternoon.

242
00:18:39.767 --> 00:18:43.599
and I want my building
looking worthy top to bottom.

243
00:18:43.767 --> 00:18:45.307
I understand. ma'am.

244
00:18:45.475 --> 00:18:47.307
If you understand.

245
00:18:47.475 --> 00:18:50.182
why are you entering your rooms?

246
00:19:00.225 --> 00:19:02.932
Let me help you!

247
00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.557
Get out of here!

248
00:19:04.725 --> 00:19:08.557
You need me. I can clean.

249
00:19:08.725 --> 00:19:10.932
In fact. 'Squeaky Clean'
is my middle name.

250
00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.266
I'm young.
My legs work. Yours don't.

251
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:18.266
Uh. it's gonna feel so much easier
with me helping.

252
00:19:26.683 --> 00:19:28.974
Are you coming?

253
00:19:30.225 --> 00:19:33.807
Whoa! That's a lot of stairs.

254
00:19:33.975 --> 00:19:36.682
- Are you the caretaker?
- Yes.

255
00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:39.682
And you can stay with me
until you get on your feet.

256
00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:42.349
on one condition -
no more questions.

257
00:19:42.517 --> 00:19:44.099
How long can I stay?

258
00:19:44.267 --> 00:19:46.266
Ugh. That was a question.

259
00:19:46.433 --> 00:19:48.932
By the way. who was that witch?

260
00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.682
Regine Le Haut.
She owns this building.

261
00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.599
And she eats ginger orphans
with ponytails.

262
00:19:54.767 --> 00:19:56.141
Now. clean!

263
00:19:58.558 --> 00:20:01.057
Huh? How long
have you worked here?

264
00:20:01.225 --> 00:20:02.849
Do you have a nickname?
Wanna know mine?

265
00:20:03.017 --> 00:20:04.932
Will I have my own bed?
What's your favourite soup?

266
00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.599
Do you snore?
Are you a morning person?

267
