to work really hard. listen.

525
00:33:43.975 --> 00:33:45.891
push yourself
and then work some more.

526
00:34:08.683 --> 00:34:13.099
- Who is that?
- Rudi from the top boys class.

527
00:34:13.267 --> 00:34:16.599
Holder of the Best Cheekbones
at the Opera award.

528
00:34:16.767 --> 00:34:20.349
I love him!
He's so blond and shiny.

529
00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:34.099
Oh. wow!

530
00:34:36.850 --> 00:34:40.932
Ooh! You are new. yes?

531
00:34:41.100 --> 00:34:42.849
Yes.

532
00:34:43.017 --> 00:34:45.807
- She's Camille.
- She has two eyes.

533
00:34:45.975 --> 00:34:51.099
Ha! You have spirit. Camille.
but your dancing sucks.

534
00:34:51.267 --> 00:34:53.391
It's mine!

535
00:34:53.558 --> 00:34:55.016
Who does he think he is?

536
00:34:55.183 --> 00:34:58.349
Until we meet again. Minoushka!

537
00:34:58.517 --> 00:34:59.891
Only in your dreams.

538
00:35:00.058 --> 00:35:01.099
Felicie?

539
00:35:01.267 --> 00:35:04.682
- What are you doing here?
- I can explain!

540
00:35:04.850 --> 00:35:07.141
There is nothing to explain.

541
00:35:08.600 --> 00:35:10.724
Wait! Wait!

542
00:35:29.017 --> 00:35:30.557
Whoa!

543
00:35:38.017 --> 00:35:40.224
I'm sorry! Triple sorry.

544
00:35:40.392 --> 00:35:43.932
If there was a bigger word
for 'sorry'. I'd say it.

545
00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:46.307
I let you into my life.
and you lied to me.

546
00:35:46.475 --> 00:35:47.849
I don't like lies.

547
00:35:48.017 --> 00:35:50.807
I could lose my job
because of you.

548
00:35:50.975 --> 00:35:53.307
I get it. I messed up.

549
00:35:53.475 --> 00:35:55.974
But you don't understand.

550
00:35:56.142 --> 00:35:59.057
Since I can remember.
I've wanted to dance.

551
00:35:59.225 --> 00:36:01.224
And when I saw Rosita Mauri

552
00:36:01.392 --> 00:36:03.266
and she did those amazing moves.

553
00:36:03.433 --> 00:36:05.307
I knew that's what
I wanted to be.

554
00:36:05.475 --> 00:36:08.141
I knew my dream could come true!

555
00:36:10.350 --> 00:36:12.807
I know it's hard to understand.

556
00:36:13.850 --> 00:36:16.141
You hate dancing.

557
00:36:16.308 --> 00:36:21.307
But I just want you to know
I'm truly sorry.

558
00:36:53.517 --> 00:36:56.807
Any mail?

559
00:36:56.975 --> 00:36:58.974
There is no mail.

560
00:37:01.308 --> 00:37:04.682
As soon as there is. fetch it.

561
00:37:06.725 --> 00:37:08.349
Can you dance?

562
00:37:08.517 --> 00:37:11.599
Yes. At least. I think I can.

563
00:37:11.767 --> 00:37:14.141
Training starts at 5am tomorrow.

564
00:37:14.308 --> 00:37:16.724
Are you a teacher?

565
00:37:16.892 --> 00:37:19.141
Do you have another option?

566
00:37:20.558 --> 00:37:22.432
5am?

567
00:37:41.392 --> 00:37:43.682
Time to train!

568
00:37:43.850 --> 00:37:45.224
Jump and ring the bell!

569
00:37:45.392 --> 00:37:46.724
- Why?
- Just do it.

570
00:37:46.892 --> 00:37:48.391
You don't want me to dance?

571
00:37:48.558 --> 00:37:51.932
No talking.
Jump and ring the bell!

572
00:37:52.100 --> 00:37:55.057
Again.

573
00:37:55.225 --> 00:37:56.849
You said we were going to train.

574
00:37:57.017 --> 00:37:59.682
- This is it! Again!
- Hmm!

575
00:37:59.850 --> 00:38:01.224
Ha!

576
00:38:01.392 --> 00:38:03.307
Felicie. you lack
precision and finesse.

577
00:38:03.475 --> 00:38:05.349
You have little
or no sense of rhythm.

578
00:38:05.517 --> 00:38:07.849
You're without balance.
grace and charm.

579
00:38:08.017 --> 00:38:11.099
Come on! You can't tell all that
from one jump. can you?

580
00:38:12.850 --> 00:38:14.224
You can.

581
00:38:14.392 --> 00:38:17.016
On the good side. you have
the energy of a bullet.

582
00:38:17.183 --> 00:38:20.099
but you also have the lightness
of a depressed elephant.

583
00:38:20.267 --> 00:38:23.141
Hey! Merante used
exactly the same phrase!

584
00:38:23.308 --> 00:38:26.349
After 10 years of cleaning.
you pick stuff up.

585
00:38:26.517 --> 00:38:28.932
OK. now jump up. ring this bell.

586
00:38:29.100 --> 00:38:31.099
land and do not
splash the water.

587
00:38:31.267 --> 00:38:32.641
But that's impossible.

588
00:38:32.808 --> 00:38:35.849
I thought it was
your dream to dance.

589
00:38:36.017 --> 00:38:38.849
OK!

590
00:38:44.600 --> 00:38:46.557
Come on!

591
00:38:52.517 --> 00:38:56.349
♪ You're so unfair to yourself

592
00:38:58.850 --> 00:39:01.557
♪ Got that feeling
in your chest... ♪

593
00:39:08.100 --> 00:39:10.932
- ♪ Can't look in the mirror... ♪
- Get lost.

594
00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:14.516
- ♪ Can't see who you are... ♪
- Get lost!

595
00:39:14.683 --> 00:39:16.057
Shoo! Shoo!

596
00:39:16.225 --> 00:39:20.099
♪ You wanna be somebody else

597
00:39:23.475 --> 00:39:27.599
♪ Every time you falter

598
00:39:27.767 --> 00:39:31.141
♪ Every time you fall

599
00:39:31.308 --> 00:39:35.974
♪ I can still see
the road ahead... ♪

600
00:39:45.850 --> 00:39:49.724
♪ You'll be brighter
than the stars

601
00:39:49.892 --> 00:39:53.766
♪ And you'll see
how radiant you are

602
00:39:53.933 --> 00:39:55.224
♪ I know you're full of doubt

603
00:39:55.392 --> 00:39:57.682
♪ But don't let them
bring you down

604
00:39:57.850 --> 00:40:01.932
♪ 'Cause you're unstoppable

605
00:40:02.100 --> 00:40:05.599
♪ Rising higher than the sun

606
00:40:05.767 --> 00:40:09.932
♪ Climb all the way to the top

607
00:40:10.100 --> 00:40:12.099
♪ Way up above the clouds

608
00:40:12.267 --> 00:40:15.057
♪ They'll never bring you down
'cause you're unstoppable... ♪

609
00:40:15.225 --> 00:40:17.932
You!

610
00:40:18.100 --> 00:40:19.557
That was not merely bad.

611
00:40:19.725 --> 00:40:21.807
it was a catastrophe
wrapped in a disaster

612
00:40:21.975 --> 00:40:24.266
with a side order of bad.

613
00:40:24.433 --> 00:40:26.474
Ta-ta!

614
00:40:30.225 --> 00:40:31.599
♪ Hold on. don't let go... ♪

615
00:40:31.767 --> 00:40:34.182
You. me. up.

616
00:40:34.350 --> 00:40:36.349
♪ Even in the dark. you glow

617
00:40:36.517 --> 00:40:40.307
♪ You'll be brighter
than the stars

618
00:40:40.475 --> 00:40:42.432
♪ And you'll see
how radiant you are... ♪

619
00:40:42.600 --> 00:40:44.807
It's incredible!

620
00:40:44.975 --> 00:40:47.349
♪ They'll never
bring you down... ♪

621
00:40:49.100 --> 00:40:50.599
♪ 'Cause you're unstoppable... ♪

622
00:40:50.767 --> 00:40:54.016
Last time we met.
I was so very rude.

623
00:40:54.183 --> 00:40:56.516
Let me introduce myself.

624
00:40:56.683 --> 00:40:59.432
I am Rudolph Dimitriev
Stanislaw Artiem Rankovsky...

625
00:40:59.600 --> 00:41:01.724
...the Third.

626
00:41:01.892 --> 00:41:04.016
Big choice of names there.

627
00:41:04.183 --> 00:41:07.224
Don't worry.
Everyone finds it hard at first.

628
00:41:07.392 --> 00:41:09.599
But you and I are unique.

629
00:41:09.767 --> 00:41:12.682
and we do not
follow silly rules. yes?

630
00:41:12.850 --> 00:41:16.682
How is that pick-up line
working out for you?

631
00:41:16.850 --> 00:41:20.182
It is no line.
I say it only to you. Camille.

632
00:41:20.350 --> 00:41:21.724
Just to you.

633
00:41:31.100 --> 00:41:33.224
Et hop!

634
00:41:33.392 --> 00:41:36.224
Minoushka!

635
00:41:42.433 --> 00:41:45.349
Uh. are you alright. Camille?

636
00:41:45.517 --> 00:41:48.099
Yep! I'm OK!

637
00:41:48.267 --> 00:41:50.599
There's this boy. Rudolph.
who. it turns out.

638
00:41:50.767 --> 00:41:52.141
is a real Russian prince

639
00:41:52.308 --> 00:41:54.557
with a castle and peacocks
and cheekbones!

640
00:41:54.725 --> 00:41:56.891
And he took me
on the roof of the Opera.

641
00:41:57.058 --> 00:42:00.099
and he was looking at me
like this.

642
00:42:00.267 --> 00:42:01.682
Then like this.

643
00:42:01.850 --> 00:42:04.932
And then once like this.

644
00:42:05.100 --> 00:42:07.807
Wait! Uh. a boy?
What type of boy?

645
00:42:07.975 --> 00:42:10.391
Peacocks?
What type of cheekbones?

646
00:42:10.558 --> 00:42:12.599
- And Rudolph?
- He's a friend.

647
00:42:12.767 --> 00:42:14.599
He says I'm gonna be
everything I wanna be.

648
00:42:14.767 --> 00:42:16.141
I say that too!

649
00:42:16.308 --> 00:42:18.349
But he's deep as well.

650
00:42:18.517 --> 00:42:22.266
Deep? Yeah. well. I have these.

651
00:42:22.433 --> 00:42:24.516
Ta-da!

652
00:42:24.683 --> 00:42:26.807
Whoo-hoo. Doors.

653
00:42:26.975 --> 00:42:29.349
Yes. the doors to the atelier

654
00:42:29.517 --> 00:42:31.349
of my new boss.
engineer. genius.

655
00:42:31.517 --> 00:42:33.682
If you saw what was
behind these doors.

656
00:42:33.850 --> 00:42:35.266
I would have to kill you.

657
00:42:35.433 --> 00:42:36.807
Ahh!

658
00:42:36.975 --> 00:42:40.099
Looks like you're gonna
have to kill me. then!

659
00:42:41.808 --> 00:42:43.349
Oh la la!

660
00:42:45.975 --> 00:42:47.432
What's that?

661
00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:50.182
The Statue of Puberty.

662
00:42:50.350 --> 00:42:53.307
soon to go to America!

663
00:42:53.475 --> 00:42:55.432
But it is a super secret.

664
00:42:55.600 --> 00:42:58.724
so you did not see it. OK?

665
00:42:58.892 --> 00:43:01.557
OK.

666
00:43:01.725 --> 00:43:03.557
So. here's my office.

667
00:43:03.725 --> 00:43:07.141
the home of big ideas
and genius.

668
00:43:07.308 --> 00:43:09.682
For example.
here we see the plans

669
00:43:09.850 --> 00:43:11.932
for chicken wings version 3.

670
00:43:12.100 --> 00:43:14.932
Oh! Aaah! Ahem!

671
00:43:15.100 --> 00:43:18.266
At the moment. my boss and I
are working on several.

672
00:43:18.433 --> 00:43:22.266
uh. important... inventions.

673
00:43:22.433 --> 00:43:25.432
He. uh. he...

674
00:43:25.600 --> 00:43:27.307
He calls me his ideas man.

675
00:43:27.475 --> 00:43:29.432
Do you know how
to use all this stuff?

676
00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:33.099
Uh. not yet.
but I... I have a chair!

677
00:43:33.267 --> 00:43:35.974
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

678
00:43:37.350 --> 00:43:38.724
Ha!

679
00:43:38.892 --> 00:43:41.182
- Oh. hey. Victor!
- He's the cleaner.

680
00:43:41.350 --> 00:43:43.974
He's two sandwiches
short of a picnic.

681
00:43:44.142 --> 00:43:48.016
So the pencils
all need sharpening.

682
00:43:48.183 --> 00:43:50.474
and the boss wants us to polish
his boots for tomorrow.

683
00:43:52.183 --> 00:43:54.432
So. your big boss calls you
his ideas man. huh?

684
00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:57.016
Well. uh.
he... he has the ideas.

685
00:43:57.183 --> 00:43:59.557
and I think they're great.

686
00:43:59.725 --> 00:44:01.849
But it's a start!

687
00:44:02.017 --> 00:44:05.099
Hey. Victor.
you were right for once.

688
00:44:05.267 --> 00:44:07.099
Dreams can come true!

689
00:44:07.267 --> 00:44:11.141
Oh! Oh! Oh no!

690
00:44:16.100 --> 00:44:17.516
First position. second.

691
00:44:17.683 --> 00:44:19.516
third. fourth. fifth.

692
00:44:19.683 --> 00:44:22.516
These five positions form
the basis of everything.

693
00:44:22.683 --> 00:44:25.182
First position. second.
third. fourth. fifth.

694
00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.724
Now you jump.

695
00:44:26.892 --> 00:44:29.266
First position. second.
third. fourth. fifth.

696
00:44:29.433 --> 00:44:31.391
And pose and smile!

697
00:44:33.683 --> 00:44:36.391
It's when you're tired
that you start to progress.

698
00:44:36.558 --> 00:44:38.849
You were a dancer. weren't you?

699
00:44:39.017 --> 00:44:41.016
No more questions.

700
00:44:41.183 --> 00:44:43.432
Again!

701
00:44:47.683 --> 00:44:51.807
Oh. to reach. you might need
to stand on your pointes.

702
00:44:52.850 --> 00:44:56.349
Feel the balance. Oh!

703
00:44:56.517 --> 00:45:00.432
Your toes must be
as flexible as willow

704
00:45:00.600 --> 00:45:02.599
and hard as a rock.

705
00:45:05.975 --> 00:45:07.016
First position!

706
00:45:07.183 --> 00:45:11.724
Uh-uh-uh! No hands allowed.

707
00:45:11.892 --> 00:45:13.349
What?

708
00:45:13.517 --> 00:45:16.266
- Try this way.
- Oh! Stop! Stop!

709
00:45:16.433 --> 00:45:17.807
Oh!

710
00:45:17.975 --> 00:45:19.849
You were a dancer. weren't you?

711
00:45:20.017 --> 00:45:21.932
Of course I was
a dancer. Sherlock Holmes.

712
00:45:23.183 --> 00:45:24.557
To pirouette.

713
00:45:24.725 --> 00:45:27.724
you must become
the mistress of your dizziness.

714
00:45:27.892 --> 00:45:31.349
Stare at a spot.
and don't ever lose it.

715
00:45:33.350 --> 00:45:37.224
OK. now come to me.
and don't spill the water.

716
00:45:40.142 --> 00:45:41.182
Whoa!

717
00:45:48.850 --> 00:45:51.016
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

718
00:45:51.183 --> 00:45:54.474
♪ When you ask me to jump

719
00:45:54.642 --> 00:45:56.016
♪ I say how high... ♪

720
00:45:56.183 --> 00:46:00.016
Try to introduce your left foot
to your right foot.

721
00:46:00.183 --> 00:46:02.849
See if they can
get along one day.

722
00:46:03.017 --> 00:46:05.349
♪ I'm waiting in line

723
00:46:05.517 --> 00:46:07.057
♪ But now that it's time... ♪

724
00:46:07.225 --> 00:46:09.682
There's a bright future for you

725
00:46:09.850 --> 00:46:12.557
as a candle seller.

726
00:46:16.475 --> 00:46:18.932
♪ I'm gonna take
what's mine... ♪

727
00:46:19.100 --> 00:46:20.974
First position!

728
00:46:21.142 --> 00:46:23.182
Second! Third!

729
00:46:23.350 --> 00:46:25.932
Fourth. and rest in fifth.

730
00:46:26.100 --> 00:46:28.349
Thank you. mam'selles.

731
00:46:35.308 --> 00:46:38.557
That was... better!

732
00:46:38.725 --> 00:46:40.557
Thanks!

733
00:46:40.725 --> 00:46:42.807
I'm ready to do
that crazy. jumpy thing.

734
00:46:42.975 --> 00:46:44.349
And I'm the Empress Josephine.

735
00:46:44.517 --> 00:46:45.391
I am!

736
00:46:45.558 --> 00:46:46.932
Of course you are.

737
00:46:47.100 --> 00:46:48.932
but there's a difference
between being ready

738
00:46:49.100 --> 00:46:50.516
and being ready to do it well.

739
00:46:50.683 --> 00:46:52.182
That's why we train every day.

740
00:46:52.350 --> 00:46:54.057
That's all we've been doing!

741
00:46:54.225 --> 00:46:56.932
And then you'll be ready when
you can answer the question.

742
00:46:57.100 --> 00:46:58.682
"Why do you dance?"

743
00:46:58.850 --> 00:47:01.307
I've answered it! It's my dream!

744
00:47:13.142 --> 00:47:14.557
Oh! Oh!

745
00:47:14.725 --> 00:47:16.557
Ow! Ow!

746
00:47:16.725 --> 00:47:18.599
Oh!

747
00:47:18.767 --> 00:47:22.266
By the way. that crazy jumpy thing
is called le grand jeté.

748
00:47:22.433 --> 00:47:23.849
and you're not ready.

749
00:47:24.017 --> 00:47:27.266
Are you doing dance or kung-fu?

750
00:47:27.433 --> 00:47:29.932
You are SO funny.

751
00:47:30.100 --> 00:47:33.099
This is Victor. We escaped
from the orphanage together.

752
00:47:33.267 --> 00:47:36.224
Hello! I am loving your apron.

753
00:47:37.433 --> 00:47:40.599
It seems that
you are going out tonight.

754
00:47:40.767 --> 00:47:41.724
Yep!

755
00:47:41.892 --> 00:47:44.807
Bring her back late
and you will be six inches smaller.

756
00:47:44.975 --> 00:47:47.141
Of course. of course. of course!

757
00:47:47.308 --> 00:47:49.391
It's a quiet. sober.

758
00:47:49.558 --> 00:47:51.307
quiet. sober thing.

759
00:47:53.017 --> 00:47:56.307
- Breton music?
- Whoa!

760
00:47:59.558 --> 00:48:01.266
Whoa! Excuse me!

761
00:48:03.725 --> 00:48:05.849
Whoo!

762
00:48:09.392 --> 00:48:11.974
- I love it here!
- Whoo!

763
00:48:12.142 --> 00:48:13.849
Let's party!

764
00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:20.016
Did you say
you loved me or the bar?

765
00:48:21.058 --> 00:48:23.641
- Yeah!
- Whoo!

766
00:48:23.808 --> 00:48:25.599
Whoa!

767
00:48:28.767 --> 00:48:31.266
Wow!

768
00:48:33.142 --> 00:48:35.141
Whoo!

769
00:48:42.225 --> 00:48:45.182
That's my girlfriend!

770
00:48:45.350 --> 00:48:46.891
You're a lucky guy!

771
00:48:58.892 --> 00:49:01.516
Oh. wow!

772
00:49:10.392 --> 00:49:12.891
Oh! Oh!

773
00:49:16.475 --> 00:49:20.266
I hope that tomorrow you act
with a little more dignity.

774
00:49:21.600 --> 00:49:26.141
Anyway. tonight was...
a good performance.

775
00:49:26.308 --> 00:49:27.849
Thank you. sir.

776
00:49:29.642 --> 00:49:32.641
- Whoo!
- Whoo-hoo!

777
00:49:32.808 --> 00:49:38.141
I have no idea why
you're happy. but it is great!

778
00:49:38.308 --> 00:49:40.974
Whoo!

779
00:49:46.600 --> 00:49:49.182
Well. I'd better go in.

780
00:49:49.350 --> 00:49:51.349
I've got my audition tomorrow.

781
00:49:51.517 --> 00:49:54.849
Of course! Sleep well.
And I... I...

782
00:49:55.017 --> 00:49:58.432
- What?
- I think you're. uh...

783
00:49:59.892 --> 00:50:01.266
I think you're great.

784
00:50:01.433 --> 00:50:03.307
Thanks.

785
00:50:11.350 --> 00:50:14.266
- What are you doing?
- Uh. oh. nothing!

786
00:50:14.433 --> 00:50:16.141
I'm stretching.

787
00:50:16.308 --> 00:50:18.016
Yeah. gotta...
Ooh. gotta get that one!

788
00:50:18.183 --> 00:50:20.432
OK! Yeah. it's best I leave.

789
00:50:22.142 --> 00:50:24.474
Stupid. stupid. stupid!

790
00:50:24.642 --> 00:50:27.266
- Hey. Victor!
- Uh-huh?

791
00:50:27.433 --> 00:50:31.474
I had the best time.

792
00:50:31.642 --> 00:50:34.391
Thanks! Goodnight. Felicie.

793
00:50:34.558 --> 00:50:38.182
Oh. sorry.
Mademoiselle Camille Le Haut.

794
00:50:56.725 --> 00:50:59.641
Wretch!

795
00:50:59.808 --> 00:51:01.849
I want her put in prison!

796
00:51:02.017 --> 00:51:06.599
She stole my life.
my honour and my name!

797
00:51:06.767 --> 00:51:09.599
I want it back!

798
00:51:09.767 --> 00:51:12.599
- Too much.
- OK.

799
00:51:12.767 --> 00:51:16.016
What is your name?

800
00:51:20.142 --> 00:51:22.349
My name is Felicie Lebras.

801
00:51:22.517 --> 00:51:25.057
I come from an orphanage
in Brittany.

802
00:51:25.225 --> 00:51:26.974
I didn't mean to hurt Camille.

803
00:51:27.142 --> 00:51:29.391
I just wanted to be
at the Opera and...

804
00:51:29.558 --> 00:51:31.557
I'm sorry.

805
00:51:31.725 --> 00:51:33.599
Madame...

806
00:51:35.475 --> 00:51:37.891
You traitor!

807
00:51:39.017 --> 00:51:41.266
You knew this!

808
00:51:41.433 --> 00:51:42.849
You stabbed me in the back!

809
00:51:43.017 --> 00:51:46.016
- You are sacked!
- Silence!

810
00:51:47.142 --> 00:51:50.349
Alright. like it or lump it.
here is my deal.

811
00:51:50.517 --> 00:51:51.891
Miss Le Haut.

812
00:51:52.058 --> 00:51:55.349
you may enter the coryphée class
starting tomorrow.

813
00:51:55.517 --> 00:51:57.391
And you will also
be in the auditions

814
00:51:57.558 --> 00:51:59.141
for the part in 'The Nutcracker'.

815
00:51:59.308 --> 00:52:00.682
But I want to be clear.

816
00:52:00.850 --> 00:52:03.432
if you sack Madame Odette.
I will sack Camille.

817
00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:05.224
You!

818
00:52:05.392 --> 00:52:08.599
You made a terrible start
to the classes.

819
00:52:08.767 --> 00:52:11.641
and you have lied
and cheated to be here.

820
00:52:13.767 --> 00:52:17.016
But you have also
shown great promise.

821
00:52:17.183 --> 00:52:20.182
and you've worked hard
and shown your dedication.

822
00:52:20.350 --> 00:52:22.891
You must have a good teacher.

823
00:52:23.058 --> 00:52:25.099
So you may also stay
in the auditions.

824
00:52:25.267 --> 00:52:27.891
If you get the part in 'The Nutcracker'
fair and square.

825
00:52:28.058 --> 00:52:30.182
you may become a coryphée too.

826
00:52:30.350 --> 00:52:33.266
If you fail to get the part.
then you must leave the Opera.

827
00:52:33.433 --> 00:52:35.016
- Is that clear?
- Yes.

828
00:52:35.183 --> 00:52:37.349
Is that also
clear to you. madame?

829
00:52:37.517 --> 00:52:39.266
Clear.

830
00:52:39.433 --> 00:52:42.474
Then. Felicie Lebras
from Brittany.

831
00:52:42.642 --> 00:52:46.182
your future at the Opera
is in your hands.

832
00:52:52.642 --> 00:52:54.182
Hmm!

833
00:52:55.892 --> 00:52:58.349
What if she's good. Mother?

834
00:52:58.517 --> 00:53:00.682
Get that part. do you hear me?

835
00:53:00.850 --> 00:53:02.391
I want vengeance.

836
00:53:03.433 --> 00:53:06.516
I will have it.

837
00:53:16.767 --> 00:53:19.224
She even makes sweeping
look graceful.

838
00:53:19.392 --> 00:53:21.224
She was a good dancer.
wasn't she?

839
00:53:21.392 --> 00:53:24.599
Not just a good dancer.
The best of her generation.

840
00:53:24.767 --> 00:53:27.766
And then there was
a fire onstage.

841
00:53:34.017 --> 00:53:35.432
Oh!

842
00:53:35.600 --> 00:53:37.391
What's this for?

843
00:53:38.767 --> 00:53:40.641
For everything!

844
00:53:40.808 --> 00:53:44.016
We don't have time for this.

845
00:53:44.183 --> 00:53:46.724
We're talking about
your future now.

846
00:53:46.892 --> 00:53:49.849
You have only one opponent -
Camille.

847
00:53:52.767 --> 00:53:55.641
I have seen her. I know her.

848
00:53:56.725 --> 00:53:58.474
Her technique is perfect.

849
00:53:58.642 --> 00:54:00.182
and she is stronger
than she looks.

850
00:54:01.767 --> 00:54:03.307
She is precise. she is sharp.

851
00:54:03.475 --> 00:54:05.974
and losing is not a word
in her vocabulary.

852
00:54:06.142 --> 00:54:07.724
Up. down! Up. down!

853
00:54:07.892 --> 00:54:10.224
Up. down! Again!

854
00:54:10.392 --> 00:54:12.724
- Up. down!
- I'm tired.

855
00:54:12.892 --> 00:54:14.266
'Tired' is for losers!

856
00:54:14.433 --> 00:54:17.474
Again! I am going
to get that part!

857
00:54:17.642 --> 00:54:20.974
If you try to take her down
on her turf. you will fail.

858
00:54:22.392 --> 00:54:25.016
Your diet suffers
from eating very little food.

859
00:54:25.183 --> 00:54:27.182
Your muscles
are like marshmallows.

860
00:54:27.350 --> 00:54:30.432
In short. on paper.
you're going to get humiliated.

861
00:54:32.933 --> 00:54:36.307
Great pep talk!
So. how do I get that part?

862
00:54:36.475 --> 00:54:39.891
You get the part
because you have something

863
00:54:40.058 --> 00:54:42.641
she can only dream of - passion!

864
00:54:51.183 --> 00:54:52.641
Build on this.

865
00:54:52.808 --> 00:54:56.599
Feel your anger and your pain
and your sorrow and your joy.

866
00:54:56.767 --> 00:54:58.641
and put it all into your dance.

867
00:54:58.808 --> 00:55:01.432
Live the music. feel it.

868
00:55:03.933 --> 00:55:06.849
Every note. every sound.
every harmony

869
00:55:07.017 --> 00:55:09.474
needs to have
your body vibrating

870
00:55:09.642 --> 00:55:13.849
from the end of your hair
to the tips of your toes.

871
00:55:14.017 --> 00:55:19.016
And then. and only then.
will you take her down.

872
00:55:27.642 --> 00:55:30.766
Alright! The person
leaving us today is...

873
00:55:36.767 --> 00:55:39.141
Ahem!

874
00:55:40.183 --> 00:55:43.432
Hmm!

875
00:55:44.767 --> 00:55:46.849
This is the end of the road.
Miss Nora.

876
00:55:47.017 --> 00:55:48.724
What road?

877
00:55:48.892 --> 00:55:50.891
Oh. I'm finished.

878
00:55:51.058 --> 00:55:53.891
I like you. Beat her.

879
00:55:54.058 --> 00:55:56.974
Camille and Felicie.
tomorrow morning at 8:00am.

880
00:55:57.142 --> 00:55:59.307
we will know which one of you
will have the honour

881
00:55:59.475 --> 00:56:02.391
of dancing Clara
in 'The Nutcracker' with Rosita.

882
00:56:02.558 --> 00:56:06.974
I can only advise you
to give everything. ladies.

883
00:56:07.142 --> 00:56:10.349
You've made lots of progress.
dirty. little rat.

884
00:56:10.517 --> 00:56:13.057
but tomorrow I am going
to be the chosen one.

885
00:56:13.225 --> 00:56:14.599
We'll see.

886
00:56:14.767 --> 00:56:16.641
You can work
as hard as you like.

887
00:56:16.808 --> 00:56:18.266
you can train 24 hours a day.

888
00:56:18.433 --> 00:56:20.891
but you will always be nothing!

889
00:56:21.058 --> 00:56:23.974
- I am somebody.
- Who exactly?

890
00:56:24.142 --> 00:56:26.057
Answer me! Who are you?

891
00:56:27.350 --> 00:56:29.974
You're nothing!

892
00:56:33.142 --> 00:56:34.932
Nothing!

893
00:56:36.808 --> 00:56:38.641
She's wrong. you know.

894
00:56:38.808 --> 00:56:40.599
- You're not alone.
- What?

895
00:56:43.017 --> 00:56:45.474
You have me.

896
00:56:45.642 --> 00:56:48.266
And I know exactly
what we are going to do.

897
00:56:48.433 --> 00:56:50.266
Tonight. to prove
our connection.

898
00:56:50.433 --> 00:56:52.849
we will embark on
a little romantic party.

899
00:56:53.017 --> 00:56:55.057
I offer you the Eiffel Tower.

900
00:56:55.225 --> 00:56:57.099
I offer you fireworks.

901
00:56:57.267 --> 00:57:00.182
- Tonight. 7:00pm.
- I should train.

902
00:57:00.350 --> 00:57:02.099
You don't need to train.

903
00:57:02.267 --> 00:57:04.141
You don't need to know
who you are.

904
00:57:04.308 --> 00:57:06.224
You are unique.

905
00:57:06.392 --> 00:57:08.057
Say that again?

906
00:57:08.225 --> 00:57:10.099
Tonight.

907
00:57:10.267 --> 00:57:13.224
Felicie. it gives me
great pleasure

908
00:57:13.392 --> 00:57:14.891
to present to you...

909
00:57:15.058 --> 00:57:16.641
No!

910
00:57:21.017 --> 00:57:23.599
Victor! I'm in
the final audition!

911
00:57:23.767 --> 00:57:25.849
Wow! Congratulations!

912
00:57:26.017 --> 00:57:29.391
I have great news too.
My boss finally spoke to me!

913
00:57:29.558 --> 00:57:33.141
He said. "Get off my foot.
you biological mutation!"

914
00:57:33.308 --> 00:57:35.891
That's good. right?

915
00:57:36.058 --> 00:57:38.974
Ugh! You have no class.

916
00:57:39.142 --> 00:57:41.599
What. me? No class?

917
00:57:41.767 --> 00:57:44.391
- Rudi has class.
- Rudi again?

918
00:57:44.558 --> 00:57:46.891
What. is he your boyfriend now?

919
00:57:47.058 --> 00:57:51.099
No! He and I. we're connected.

920
00:57:51.267 --> 00:57:53.057
OK. OK. You win!

921
00:57:53.225 --> 00:57:57.141
I'll give you class
and connectivity-ness.

922
00:57:57.308 --> 00:57:59.057
Dinner! You and me.

923
00:57:59.225 --> 00:58:01.182
Some knives and forks. napkins.

924
00:58:01.350 --> 00:58:05.016
Uh. 7:00pm. north leg
of the Eiffel Tower.

925
00:58:05.183 --> 00:58:08.141
Is that a yes?

926
00:58:11.017 --> 00:58:12.724
Yeah.

927
00:58:12.892 --> 00:58:14.432
That's a yes.

928
00:58:14.600 --> 00:58:17.766
Sit! I've got something for you.

929
00:58:20.017 --> 00:58:23.057
They were mine.
Now they're yours.

930
00:58:23.225 --> 00:58:25.724
Wow! Thanks.

931
00:58:25.892 --> 00:58:27.307
OK. enough talking.

932
00:58:27.475 --> 00:58:29.432
Eat. and then we practise
for tomorrow.

933
00:58:29.600 --> 00:58:31.766
What?

934
00:58:31.933 --> 00:58:35.641
Well. I'm going out with Rudi.

935
00:58:35.808 --> 00:58:40.141
He says I'm ready.
He says I'm unique.

936
00:58:40.308 --> 00:58:42.557
Why do you dance?

937
00:58:42.725 --> 00:58:44.724
Stop asking me that question!

938
00:58:44.892 --> 00:58:48.349
When I was a dancer.
the night before an audition.

939
00:58:48.517 --> 00:58:50.141
I trained and then I rested.

940
00:58:50.308 --> 00:58:52.557
- Rudi's waiting for me.
- Stay!

941
00:58:52.725 --> 00:58:55.224
No! You're not my mom!

942
00:58:55.392 --> 00:58:57.599
I'm sorry. I wasn't thinking.

943
00:58:57.767 --> 00:58:59.474
OK. Go. then.

944
00:59:22.767 --> 00:59:25.557
Look at the bird.

945
00:59:25.725 --> 00:59:26.724
Um...

946
00:59:26.892 --> 00:59:29.516
No! Look at me.
Look at the bird.

947
00:59:29.683 --> 00:59:32.057
No! Hmm? Look at me.

948
00:59:32.225 --> 00:59:34.724
This is a poem I composed
in your honour.

949
00:59:34.892 --> 00:59:37.641
Ah. of course. a poem.

950
00:59:37.808 --> 00:59:39.599
"Look at the bird!

951
00:59:39.767 --> 00:59:41.474
"He flies in the sky.

952
00:59:41.642 --> 00:59:43.349
"No-one can trap him."

953
00:59:49.433 --> 00:59:50.849
Do you like?

954
00:59:51.017 --> 00:59:53.099
That's. uh...

955
00:59:53.267 --> 00:59:55.724
...well. original.

956
00:59:55.892 --> 00:59:58.599
I know. Thank you.
Come on. Minoushka!

957
00:59:58.767 --> 01:00:01.724
Let us go to the very top!
To the stars!

958
01:00:01.892 --> 01:00:05.057
OK. Matty. we practise.

959
01:00:05.225 --> 01:00:07.641
Music. please! Classical!

960
01:00:07.808 --> 01:00:11.724
OK. but that's not
my musical comfort zone.

961
01:00:11.892 --> 01:00:14.016
Oh. stop!

962
01:00:14.183 --> 01:00:16.016
Stop. stop. stop!

963
01:00:16.183 --> 01:00:18.724
We'll go Breton.
but soft and romantic.

964
01:00:18.892 --> 01:00:21.057
This will blow her away.

965
01:00:21.225 --> 01:00:23.307
She arrives. she giggles.

966
01:00:23.475 --> 01:00:26.057
I am looking dark
and mysterious.

967
01:00:26.225 --> 01:00:28.057
I give her the music box.

968
01:00:28.225 --> 01:00:31.349
She's... "Oh! Oh!" Overwhelmed!

969
01:00:31.517 --> 01:00:34.474
Uh. I don't know much
about girls.

970
01:00:34.642 --> 01:00:36.724
Frankly. they are
a mystery to me.

971
01:00:36.892 --> 01:00:40.182
But I do know that
this one's not coming.

972
01:00:40.350 --> 01:00:43.724
Young. innocent fool!
Of course she will come!

973
01:00:43.892 --> 01:00:46.974
I can already smell her perfume.

974
01:00:52.767 --> 01:00:56.182
Oh. no! Oh. beggars! Ugh!

975
01:00:56.350 --> 01:00:59.307
Paris is infested
with beggars! Yuck!

976
01:00:59.475 --> 01:01:00.891
- But...
- Don't be afraid.

977
01:01:01.058 --> 01:01:02.849
- But...
- Quiet! Follow me.

978
01:01:03.017 --> 01:01:06.599
Have no fear. I have developed
a fighting technique

979
01:01:06.767 --> 01:01:08.849
based on Cossack dancing.

980
01:01:09.017 --> 01:01:10.724
Don't be ridiculous!

981
01:01:13.892 --> 01:01:16.766
OK. stop right there!
He's my friend!

982
01:01:16.933 --> 01:01:18.599
Oh. is this some kind of joke?

983
01:01:18.767 --> 01:01:21.307
No! This is Victor.
We grew up together.

984
01:01:21.475 --> 01:01:23.849
Oh. my! This is funny.

985
01:01:24.017 --> 01:01:25.141
Friends. huh?

986
01:01:25.308 --> 01:01:27.724
If we're friends.
why are you looking so ashamed?

987
01:01:27.892 --> 01:01:30.891
- I'm not looking ashamed.
- Oh. yes. you are!

988
01:01:31.058 --> 01:01:33.557
I feel sorry for you. Felicie.

989
01:01:34.975 --> 01:01:37.266
- Oh! You're jealous.
- No!

990
01:01:37.433 --> 01:01:39.766
Ever since you started
at the Opera.

991
01:01:39.933 --> 01:01:41.724
who are you trying to be?

992
01:01:41.892 --> 01:01:44.724
Mixing with this
big. hairy asparagus?

993
01:01:44.892 --> 01:01:47.516
- You're so sad.
- Whoa. whoa. whoa!

994
01:01:49.225 --> 01:01:52.766
I could knock you out
with one flick of my tiny finger.

995
01:01:52.933 --> 01:01:56.599
but that would make my finger
dirty and smelly.

996
01:01:56.767 --> 01:02:01.266
So. I'm dirty. but at least
I don't spend my day in tights!

997
01:02:01.433 --> 01:02:03.016
I can't believe this!

998
01:02:03.183 --> 01:02:04.849
She is MY muse.

999
01:02:05.017 --> 01:02:07.724
Yeah. well. she is my
whatever-you-just-said. too.

1000
01:02:07.892 --> 01:02:10.182
with knobs on. asparagus!

1001
01:02:14.058 --> 01:02:16.891
Stop!

1002
01:02:17.058 --> 01:02:19.141
You're both idiots!

1003
01:02:23.142 --> 01:02:24.724
OK.

1004
01:02:24.892 --> 01:02:26.807
Well. goodbye. then.

1005
01:02:27.892 --> 01:02:30.182
Well. goodbye.

1006
01:02:32.850 --> 01:02:36.141
That is so low!

1007
01:03:33.308 --> 01:03:36.057
Oh. no! The audition!

1008
01:03:39.350 --> 01:03:41.057
Hmm...

1009
01:03:41.225 --> 01:03:43.891
- I'm sure this...
- Watch it!

1010
01:03:44.058 --> 01:03:46.474
...production of 'Nutcracker'
is going to...

1011
01:03:46.642 --> 01:03:49.474
Excuse me!

1012
01:03:49.642 --> 01:03:51.182
Hmm...

1013
01:03:53.142 --> 01:03:54.224
Hey!

1014
01:04:00.933 --> 01:04:03.849
Bravo! Bravo!

1015
01:04:04.017 --> 01:04:05.641
Thank you. mademoiselle.

1016
01:04:05.808 --> 01:04:07.432
The orphan is late. It's over.

1017
01:04:07.600 --> 01:04:09.016
Ahem!

1018
01:04:09.183 --> 01:04:12.891
Well. as Felicie did not deign
to show up for the audition.

1019
01:04:13.058 --> 01:04:15.474
it is Camille who will dance
with Rosita.

1020
01:04:15.642 --> 01:04:17.599
Wait! Wait! I'm here!

1021
01:04:17.767 --> 01:04:20.474
Please. please let me dance.

1022
01:04:20.642 --> 01:04:22.557
It's over! Don't you understand?

1023
01:04:22.725 --> 01:04:24.974
Sit down!

1024
01:04:25.142 --> 01:04:28.349
- I... I apologise.
- Did you sleep?

1025
01:04:28.517 --> 01:04:30.724
Not much.

1026
01:04:31.808 --> 01:04:33.224
Did you train yesterday?

1027
01:04:33.392 --> 01:04:35.974
- No.
- Why?

1028
01:04:40.267 --> 01:04:42.224
Alright. music!

1029
01:04:51.558 --> 01:04:53.349
Hmm!

1030
01:04:59.767 --> 01:05:02.849
- Start again.
- She fell! She's eliminated!

1031
01:05:03.017 --> 01:05:05.141
Start again!

1032
01:05:19.308 --> 01:05:20.724
You remember our deal?

1033
01:05:23.017 --> 01:05:25.307
Camille.
you will have the honour

1034
01:05:25.475 --> 01:05:27.307
of dancing Clara
in 'The Nutcracker'.

1035
01:05:40.017 --> 01:05:42.974
Did you think it would end here.
little rat?

1036
01:05:43.142 --> 01:05:46.766
No! Let me go! No!

1037
01:05:46.933 --> 01:05:48.807
Oh. no!

1038
01:05:50.225 --> 01:05:54.349
Please! Please!

1039
01:05:54.517 --> 01:05:56.766
Odette! No!

1040
01:05:56.933 --> 01:05:58.766
Odette!

1041
01:05:58.933 --> 01:06:00.391
Felicie!

1042
01:06:00.558 --> 01:06:02.724
You will never see her again.

1043
01:06:02.892 --> 01:06:06.141
And. of course. you're sacked.

1044
01:06:27.017 --> 01:06:29.391
Stop!

1045
01:06:29.558 --> 01:06:32.224
Where is Felicie?

1046
01:06:32.392 --> 01:06:34.766
Ahem!

1047
